s. Astra checked the calculations and technical interpretation; Terra reviewed the prose; the lead judged the proposed changes.\n\nCalculated secondary power reaches 137.08 W at 13.69 V and 10.01 A, with voltage droop. None of these points reached thermal equilibrium. The new scope data is excluded. R3 identifies the input-bridge area and R1 the secondary area. The inconsistent input reading in Capture 017 is flagged in the table.\n\n## Downloads\n\n- **Thesis_V1_V2_V3.pdf** — complete 496-page thesis, including the new V2 section on PDF pages 120–125 (printed pages 98–103).\n- **Thesis_V1_V2_V3_Source.zip** — all 566 current thesis source files, including original measurements and thermal images.\n- **Thesis_Local_Handoff.zip** — complete local-work bundle: thesis source and final PDF, current firmware/web app, imported skills, original source archives and tooling/review records.\n- **LOCAL_START.md** — instructions for continuing locally; toolchains and dependency caches must be installed locally.\n- **SHA256SUMS.txt** and **LOCAL_HANDOFF_SHA256.txt** — download checksums.\n\nThe full thesis compiled successfully. References, appendices, schematics, image integrity and ZIP member hashes were checked. Existing underfull-box and math-font substitution warnings remain; no undefined references, missing glyphs or overflowing boxes were found.\n\nExtract the local-work bundle into a new directory. The automatic GitHub “Source code” archives still reflect the older reference checkout. Use the named source or local-handoff ZIP above for the current work.\n"}